# Rust build output — large, machine-specific, and (per this phase's own
# design, see main.rs's top doc comment) already tied to one checkout path,
# so there's nothing worth committing here anyway.
src-tauri/target/
# Tauri's generated schema/binding files, regenerated on every build.
src-tauri/gen/
# Phase 11b (PARITY #52): the relocatable server bundle
# build-server-resources.mjs generates before packaging — large (~100MB+,
# mostly node-pty's per-platform prebuilds), machine/OS-specific, and
# entirely reproducible from the real source it's built from. The two
# `.gitkeep` files ARE tracked (see the negated patterns below) — Tauri's
# build script checks that `bundle.resources`' declared paths exist even
# for a plain `cargo check`/`cargo tauri dev`, not only `tauri build`, so a
# fresh checkout needs these directories to be present before anyone has
# run the bundling script.
#
# Note the shape of these rules. Un-ignoring a DIRECTORY re-admits
# everything inside it — `!.../server-bundle/` on its own would have
# committed all 98 generated files, duplicating the real server source into
# the repo. So each directory is un-ignored, its contents are ignored
# again, and only then is the `.gitkeep` un-ignored. Removing any one of
# those three lines per directory silently starts committing the bundle.
src-tauri/resources/*
!src-tauri/resources/server-bundle/
src-tauri/resources/server-bundle/*
!src-tauri/resources/server-bundle/.gitkeep
!src-tauri/resources/web/
src-tauri/resources/web/*
!src-tauri/resources/web/.gitkeep
